From e514d42f3d4f07b5b8d271442f49b31d933093f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wenbo Ji <36562829+fusheng-ji@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 13:07:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(qwen3-next): fixed-order route-weight gradient in
 combine_routes

The autograd backward of combine_routes summed grad * expert_output over H
with torch.sum, whose reduction order depends on the batch shape, so the
route-weight gradient stopped being batch-invariant from 16 rows up. Add a
custom autograd Function that sums H with fixed_order_row_sum, and a test that
compares the first 8 rows alone against the same rows inside larger batches.

Signed-off-by: Wenbo Ji <36562829+fusheng-ji@users.noreply.github.com>
